cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the paper below."
title: "chorbwo: MDP-BWO for QoS-aware service choreography in the Internet of Things"
abstract: >-
  Replication package for MDP-BWO: a learned three-state Markov model of each candidate service
  drives both a forecast-guided Black Widow Optimization search over choreography bindings and a
  per-participant finite-horizon MDP rebinding policy executed at run time as a table lookup.
  Includes the simulator, the instance generator, the baselines, the frozen protocol, the raw run
  records and the scripts that regenerate every table and figure of the paper.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Salarsefat/chorbwo"
keywords:
  - Internet of Things
  - service choreography
  - quality of service
  - Markov decision process
  - Black Widow Optimization
  - runtime adaptation
